Completion:
We are given the determinant:

$$
D(\theta) = \begin{vmatrix} 
1 & 1 & 1 \\ 
1 & 1 + \sin\theta & 1 \\ 
1 + \cos\theta & 1 & 1 
\end{vmatrix}
$$

and we are to **find the maximum value** of this determinant as $\theta$ ranges over all real angles.

---

### Step 1: Expand the determinant

We expand the $3 \times 3$ determinant using cofactor expansion along the first row.

$$
D(\theta) = 1 \cdot \begin{vmatrix} 1+\sin\theta & 1 \\ 1 & 1 \end{vmatrix}
- 1 \cdot \begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ 1+\cos\theta & 1 \end{vmatrix}
+ 1 \cdot \begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1+\sin\theta \\ 1+\cos\theta & 1 \end{vmatrix}
$$

Compute each $2 \times 2$ determinant:

1. $\begin{vmatrix} 1+\sin\theta & 1 \\ 1
